You zapped yourself with a wand of cancellation. Even worse, your
wands will all turn to dust when zapped, unless recharged first via
PYEC/scroll of charging (worth it for polymorph and wishing, not worth
it for rest), all your armor will be +0, and all magical tools will
lose their charges.

Bags of tricks and wands of cancellation are evil, evil, evil.
[SPOILER] Here's how to *properly* identify them.
Wand of cancellation:
[E]ngrave "x". Then [E] with the wand. If "The engraving on the floor
vanishes!" the wand is either cancellation, teleport, and make
invisible. To make sure, zap the wand at a junk item identified as
cursed. If the curse vanishes, the wand was cancellation. If nothing
happens, it's make invisible. If the object disappears, the wand was
teleportation. This uses two charges but will fully identify the wand.

Bag of tricks:
#loot it. If it bites you, it's a bag of tricks. :) The damage is at
most 10 HP, so don't do this at EXP:1.

Most importantly, *do not ever* put an unidentified wand in a bag that
might be a bag of holding. Do not put a bag of tricks inside a bag of
holding.  Instead, put such items in a spare [oilskin] sack. And once
you get into late game, there is almost no incentive to carry either
item anyway: the only emergency use of a wand of cancellation is to
uncurse a cursed bag of holding, which can also be managed with a
blessed scroll of remove curse or holy water in a spare sack unless
your bag is so damn heavy that you can't lift it once dropped. This is
hard to manage unless you're poorly prepared for the endgame, as even
a dozen potions of full healing plus a full assortment of attack/
teleport wands won't encumber you that much.

[/SPOILER]

As for what to do now, if you've killed the monsters, then you will
need better equipment fast, so I'd head upstairs. Consider polypiling
the blank materials after blessing them if you have a wand of
polymorph.


